# A call sweeps its own service's answers, and no other service's
# ([LCRS.6.2.1]).
#
# `svc.a` answers `ReplyA`, `svc.b` answers `ReplyB`; the rule calls `svc.a`
# as "c1". Both replies arrive with corr "c1" and both stay live: an arriving
# answer supersedes its own schema and `CallError` alone ([LCRS.6.2.4]). The
# rule fires again and its call retracts the `ReplyA`; the `ReplyB` survives.
#
#   Early  logs "early a 1", "early b 2"
#   Late   logs "late b 2"
#
# The vector LCRS.6.2.1_other_service_reply_survives pins the sweep against
# the clause; this holds the runtimes to each other.
assert Trig k=1 n=0
pump
assert ReplyA corr="c1" v=1
assert ReplyB corr="c1" v=2
assert Early k=1
pump
assert Trig k=1 n=1
pump
assert Late k=1
pump
